 "text": "Hi, how are you doing these days? Sure. It's any color named after an opposite hue after they're removed from the same color wheel. So blue and yellow, for example, are complementary to each other. It matters because these pairs of colors look where they come alive against each other. They make each other stand out, and they make anything worn or placed between them pop. You could, but black is still the strongest shadow color. Complements are best used for contrast, not for everything. You save ten bucks on raw box of black if you buy a mid tonnage white for it too. Complementary red would be one way to go.",
